EAST BAY FOUNDERS WEEKLY
Friday, March 20, 2026

Hi all. What's happening for founders in Oakland, Berkeley, Emeryville and Alameda this week.

BREAKFAST RECAP
Twenty-three people this morning, two intros made on the spot, one member hired a contractor from across the table, and the bakery ran out of the almond croissants by 8:20am. We will order more next time. Thank you to everyone who came; the next one is in May.

APRIL, TENTATIVELY
- Demo Night returns Thursday April 9, Jack London Square. Presenter sign-ups open Monday.
- A hardware-founders roundtable at the Uptown machine shop, date to be set.
- A session on hiring your first salesperson with three members who have done it, mid-April, online.

NEWS
The city small-business grant deadline is April 15. Two members have asked for help with the application; a member who received one last round has offered to review drafts. Reply and we will connect you.

Uptown coworking's first week: about 60 desks taken of 140, and the machine shop already has a waitlist for the CNC router on weekends. The coffee is reportedly good.

MEMBER NEWS
- A member's logistics-software company found its two manufacturers for the advisory day through this list. Two for two on asks this month.
- A consumer-app member is looking for beta testers who own more than ten houseplants. You know who you are.
- Congratulations to the two members who got into the spring cohort of a well-known accelerator; the East Bay is well represented this year.

JOB BOARD: 18 open roles, the most since November. https://eastbayfounders.org/jobs

Have a good weekend.

